-- title:
--   Existence of a good Néron identity component for J₀(p)
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a natural number carrying a `Fact` that it is prime. The assertion is that the type `JZeroNeronIdentityComponentGood p` is nonempty, i.e. that one can produce all of the following data. First, the data of a `JZeroNeronIdentityComponent p`: a scheme $G$ with a morphism $g : G \to \operatorname{Spec} \mathbf{Z}$, a relative group law $L$ on $g$ over $\mathbf{Z}$, and a bijection `pts` between the group `JZero p` and the sections of $g$ over $\operatorname{Spec}$ of an algebraic closure of $\mathbf{Q}$, subject to: $L$ commutative; $g$ smooth, separated, locally of finite type, quasi-compact and surjective, with preconnected fibres over every point of $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbf{Z}$; `pts` additive for $L$ and equivariant for the action of $\operatorname{Gal}$ on points; each element of `HeckeAlg` realised by an endomorphism of $g$ respecting $L$ and matching the Hecke action on `JZero p`; multiplication by each $n > 0$ flat and surjective; the subgroup generated by the integral sections of finite index in the Galois-fixed part of `JZero p`; and further conditions of the same kind, summarised here. Second, for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid p$, a `GoodPrimeData`: a relative group law $L'$ and a point dictionary `pts'` on the base change of $g$ along $\mathbf{Z} \to$ [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt ℓ`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8), compatible with $L$ and `pts` via the projection, commutative, additive and Galois-equivariant, together with an `AbelianSchemePropertyBundle` for that base change, Hecke endomorphisms of it, and, for every valuation subring $A'$ of the algebraic closure lying over $\ell$, points over $A'$ and over the residue field of $A'$ which agree with `pts'`, are additive, and satisfy the reduction-of-points identity modulo $\ell$ whenever `ReductionInputsModL` holds; the remaining fields are summarised here.
--
--   This is the existence statement for the Néron identity component of the Jacobian $J_0(p)$ over $\mathbf{Z}$, packaged together with the good-reduction data at every prime $\ell \nmid p$ which the residue and reduction arguments consume. It is the input to [`ModularCurve.nonempty_jZeroNeronIdentityComponent`](thm.html#ModularCurve.nonempty_jZeroNeronIdentityComponent), obtained from it by forgetting the good-prime fields, and to the criterion [`ModularCurve.hasJZeroNeronTorsionSheaf_two_residue_iff_reductionModL_of_dvd_eisensteinNumerator_v5`](thm.html#ModularCurve.hasJZeroNeronTorsionSheaf_two_residue_iff_reductionModL_of_dvd_eisensteinNumerator_v5).
